(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    M001 formalizes CONSTRUCTIVE REGULATOR THEORY: a finite, syntactic,
    checker-first proof system for closed implication/falsity formulas.

    The object language is deliberately small:

      A, B ::= Bot | Imp A B

    There are no object-level atoms, no object-level substitution operation,
    and no semantic truth predicate. M001 defines formulas, contexts, axiom
    sets, proof scripts, Boolean checking, checked derivability, inductive
    derivability, symbolic regulators, and evaluation-closure interfaces.

    The package is constructive. It provides deduction, constructive negation
    introduction, modus-ponens composition, syntactic adequacy, negative
    precomposition, symbolic-regulator adequacy, and evaluation-frame bridges.
    It does not provide arithmetic provability predicates, modal provability
    machinery, semantic validity, external model theory, or diagonal
    self-recognition.


