                      └──────────────────────────────────┘

    State: 7, Serviceable.

    Evaluation: Effective, mechanized, documented. Proof tactics and prose are 
    not optimal. Not peer reviewed.


3 - Intuition
    ---------

    M001 starts with formulas built only from bottom and implication:

      Formula = Bot | Imp Formula Formula

    A regulator theory supplies the logical profile and the extra axiom source:

      RegulatorTheory = RegulatorLogicProfile + AxiomSet

    A proof is a finite list of lines. Each line states a formula and cites one
    of three justifications:

      J_Assumption
      J_Axiom
      J_MP i j

    The Boolean checker validates the script against a regulator theory, a
    context, and a requested conclusion:

      regulator_theory_check_bool R Gamma p A = true

    This is the operational core. The checker rejects empty scripts, checks
    that modus-ponens references point into the already-checked prefix, and
    accepts either certificate ordering of the two MP premises. The closure
    principle exposed later remains ordinary modus ponens.

    Above the checker, M001 constructs proof transformers:

      regulator_theory_deduction_transform A p
      regulator_theory_reductio_transform A p
      regulator_theory_mp_compose B p_imp p_arg

    The deduction transformer turns a checked proof of `B` from `A :: Gamma`
    into a checked proof of `Imp A B` from `Gamma`. Constructive reductio is
    deduction at bottom, so a checked proof of `Bot` from `A :: Gamma` yields a
    checked proof of `formula_negation A = Imp A Bot`. This is not classical
    reductio and not double-negation elimination.

    The adequacy layer proves that Boolean checking and the inductive closure
    generated by assumptions, available axioms, and modus ponens coincide:

      regulator_theory_checked_derivable_iff_inductive_derivable_lemma

    The symbolic-regulator layer then reifies valid proof instructions and
    regulated proof scripts, while preserving the same checked derivability
    meaning. The closure layer exposes the same regulator as a predicate:

      regulator_theory_closure R Gamma A

    Finally, the evaluation-closure layer packages an abstract evaluator whose
    completeness names formula-valued behaviors up to regulator equivalence.
    M001 stops at this bridge. L001 is the downstream package that interprets
    the bridge as a fixed-point and obstruction theorem.


