5 - Files
    -----

    M001_00_Premises.v

      Canonical definitions for formulas, contexts, axiom sets, regulator
      profiles, regulator theories, Boolean environments, justifications,
      proof lines, and proof scripts.

    M001_01__Kernel.v

      Formula equality, context membership, finite axiom-set membership, K/S
      and optional EFQ recognition, proof-line validation, proof-script
      checking, and finite axiom-set checking.

    M001_02__Abstraction.v

      Executable deduction transformer and checked deduction theorem.

    M001_03__Falsity.v

      Object-language negation, constructive reductio, and reductio
      certificate surfaces.

    M001_04__Certificates.v

      Checked proof certificates and checked derivability vocabulary.

    M001_05__Application.v

      Proof-script shifting, checked modus-ponens composition, and checked
      closure lemmas for assumptions and axioms.

    M001_06__Syntactic_Adequacy.v

      Inductive derivability and checked/inductive adequacy.

    M001_07__Obstruction.v

      Negative transport through checked implications, context monotonicity,
      regulator-theory monotonicity, finite axiom-set monotonicity, and
      antitone non-derivability transport.

    M001_08__Regulation.v

      Regulator instructions, regulator components, regulated proof scripts,
      symbolic regulator records, finite and abstract regulator instances,
      checker/regulator equivalence, and the minimal closure/equivalence
      interface used by the evaluation and L001 layers.

    M001_09__Evaluation_Closure.v

      Generic and regulator evaluation frames, fixed-point lemmas, and
      fixed-point-free frame obstruction forms.

    M001_95_API.v

      Public operational API for the completed M001 stack.

    M001_97_Artifacts.v

      Assumption-report hooks and extraction boundary. The extracted source
      artifact is `regulator_theory_checker.ml/.mli`.

    M001_98_Sanity.v

      Smoke tests for syntax, checking, proof transformers, certificates,
      adequacy, negative transport, symbolic regulators, closure, and
      evaluation.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Extracted OCaml checker package:
      `regulator_theory_checker.{ml,mli}`.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Redirect target for the M001 assumption reports.


6 - API
    ---

    The public theorem surface is exposed by

      `From M001 Require Import M001_95_API.`

    Public surface by use case:

    Primitive syntax and theories:

      Formula, Bot, Imp                                                     (00)
      Context, ctx_empty, ctx_extend                                        (00)
      AxiomSet, FiniteAxiomSet                                              (00)
      RegulatorLogicProfile, RegulatorTheory                                (00)
      Justification, ProofLine, Proof                                       (00)

    Boolean checking:

      formula_eq_bool                                                       (01)
      ctx_mem_bool                                                          (01)
      available_axiom_bool                                                  (01)
      proof_line_valid_bool                                                 (01)
      proof_script_check_from_bool                                          (01)
      regulator_theory_check_bool                                           (01)
      finite_axiom_set_check_bool                                           (01)

    Proof transformers and certificates:

      regulator_theory_deduction_transform                                  (02)
      regulator_theory_reductio_transform                                   (03)
      regulator_theory_mp_compose                                           (05)
      regulator_theory_checked_derivable                                    (04)
      regulator_theory_not_checked_derivable                                (04)

    Closure, symbolic regulator, and evaluation:

      regulator_theory_inductive_derivable                                  (06)
      regulator_theory_closure                                              (08)
      regulator_theory_equivalent                                           (08)
      SymbolicRegulator                                                     (08)
      SymbolicRegulatorWorld                                                (08)
      EvaluationFrame                                                       (09)
      RegulatorEvaluationFrame                                              (09)

    Certified theorems:

      regulator_theory_deduction_checked :
        checked proof from A :: Gamma of B ->
        checked proof from Gamma of Imp A B

      regulator_theory_reductio_checked :
        checked proof from A :: Gamma of Bot ->
        checked proof from Gamma of formula_negation A

      regulator_theory_checked_derivable_iff_inductive_derivable_lemma :
        checked derivability and inductive derivability coincide

      regulator_theory_closure_closed_under_mp_lemma :
        regulator closure is closed under object-level modus ponens

      regulator_evaluation_frame_fixed_point_lemma :
        regulator evaluation completeness yields an equivalence fixed point


7 - Notes
    -----

    M001 is intentionally syntactic and operational. It extracts executable
    checking and proof-transformer code, but it does not extract a semantic
    validator, a model, a modal provability predicate, arithmetic coding, or an
    IO protocol.

    The sanity file is the quickest local smoke test for the package surface:

      From M001 Require Import M001_98_Sanity.

    Downstream developments should normally import `M001_95_API`; L001 does
    this and then builds the Aporetic fixed-point theorem over
    `RegulatorClosure` and `RegulatorClosureEvaluationFrame`.
